{"book":"fractions","bookTitle":"Fractions","concept":6,"title":"Adding and subtracting fractions","grades":"Grades 6–7","goal":"I can add and subtract fractions using a common denominator.","teach":"You can only add or take away parts of the <b>same size</b>. Find a common denominator, rewrite each fraction, then add or subtract the numerators. Keep the denominator. Simplify your answer.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:614px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 472 36\"><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"34.3\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"67.7\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"101.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"134.3\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"167.7\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"201.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"234.3\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><line x1=\"240.3\" y1=\"7.0\" x2=\"261.7\" y2=\"29.0\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"261.7\" y1=\"7.0\" x2=\"240.3\" y2=\"29.0\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"267.7\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><line x1=\"273.7\" y1=\"7.0\" x2=\"295.0\" y2=\"29.0\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"295.0\" y1=\"7.0\" x2=\"273.7\" y2=\"29.0\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"301.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"334.3\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"367.7\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"33.3\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><text x=\"440.0\" y=\"17.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">7</text><line x1=\"430.3\" y1=\"20.0\" x2=\"449.7\" y2=\"20.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><text x=\"440.0\" y=\"33.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">12</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">Start with 9 twelfths and take away 2 twelfths: 7 twelfths are left.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Calculate <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span> − <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span>.","steps":["The lowest common denominator of 4 and 6 is 12.","<span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">9</span><span class=\"d\">12</span></span> and <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">12</span></span>.","<span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">9</span><span class=\"d\">12</span></span> − <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">12</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">7</span><span class=\"d\">12</span></span>."]},"watch":"Do <b>not</b> add or subtract the denominators. <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> + <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span> is not <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span>.","qs":[{"text":"Fill in the missing fraction: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span> + ___ = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">9</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span>. The bar is marked in tenths.","vis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:523px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 402 36\"><rect x=\"1.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"41.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"81.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"121.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"161.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"201.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"241.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"281.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"321.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"361.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/></svg></span></div>","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Missing fraction","a":"1/2","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Change two fifths into tenths. How many more tenths make nine tenths?","steps":"1. Rule: to compare, add or subtract fractions, first write them with a common denominator (the LCM of the denominators).<br>2. <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span><br>3. missing = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">9</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span> − <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span><br>4. = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span>"},{"text":"Calculate <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">7</span></span> + <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">7</span></span>.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"The denominators are the same. Add only the numerators.","steps":"1. Formula: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> + <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a + b</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span>. Add the numerators; the denominator stays the same.<br>2. The denominators are the same, so add the numerators: 2 + 3 = 5.<br>3. Keep the denominator 7: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"d\">7</span></span>."},{"text":"Calculate <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span> − <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span>.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"Answer"}],"hint":"Change one third into sixths first.","steps":"1. Rule: to compare, add or subtract fractions, first write them with a common denominator (the LCM of the denominators).<br>2. <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span><br>3. Formula: <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> + <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a + b</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> and <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> − <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">a − b</span><span class=\"d\">c</span></span>. Add or subtract the numerators only; the denominator stays the same.<br>4. <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span> − <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span><br>5. = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span>"}]}